# ── SIR VERT ENTERPRISE — environment ─────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in your values. NEVER commit ".env".

# Storage:
#   • No token set  → data is saved to a local JSON file (data/store.json).
#     Great for local dev and any host with a writable disk.
#   • Token set     → data is saved to Vercel Blob (durable, shared across all
#     serverless instances). Required for orders to persist on Vercel.
# On Vercel: create a Blob store (Storage → Blob) and connect it to the project;
# Vercel injects BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN automatically — you don't paste it here.
# For local testing against Blob, copy the token from the Vercel dashboard:
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN="vercel_blob_rw_xxxxxxxx"

# Admin password for the /admin dashboard (defaults to "admin123" if unset — change this in production!)
# ADMIN_PASSWORD="choose-a-strong-password"
